# .cursorrules

**For Cursor (and similar agents):** Primary guidance is [AGENTS.md](./AGENTS.md). Read it first. This file is a short, current-rules companion — not a changelog. Mirror: [.antigravityrules](./.antigravityrules).

- Role: Senior Software Architect & Expert Game Developer
- Stack: TypeScript (strict, zero `any`), React 19, HTML5 Canvas 2D
- Styling: monospace retro; `App.css` / `index.css` (no UI kit, no Tailwind)
- Language: reply in French (Québécois preferred), even if the user writes in English

## Core Principles

1. Never mix React state with the Canvas high-frequency loop. React owns `GamePhase`, players, money, shop, HUD. GameEngine owns physics, terrain, projectiles, drawing, combat audio.
2. Modular, strongly-typed TypeScript. Shared types go in `src/types/`.
3. Physics at fixed 120 Hz, decoupled from display raf.
4. RNG: `secureRandom` from `src/utils/random.ts` — never `Math.random`.

## Game Specs (current)

- Loop: `requestAnimationFrame` + `PHYSICS_DT = 1/120` in `GameEngine`.
- Terrain: custom heightmap in `Terrain.ts` (multi-octaves, bumps/creux). Materials (`src/types/terrain.ts`): `DIRT` (normal), `ROCK` (indestructible stone wall for side blast; exploding on top: +50% blast, radius unaffected), `SOFT` (2.5x destruction). DRILLER: oriented shaft (`destroyTerrainShaft`, `DRILLER_SHAFT_DEPTH` = 53). GRENADE: ~2× bounce on ROCK; first contact on SOFT sticks and detonates (`grenadeBounceParams`).
- Spawns: shuffled X biased toward hollows, 100 px gap, 13 % margins, `Y = groundY`. Local humans: −25 % on SOFT. AI all modes: −25 % on ROCK (`spawnAcceptsMaterial`).
- Players: 2–4, any mix Human / `v1-random` (IA SIMPLE) / `v2-heuristic` (IA OK) / `v3-sniper` (IA SNIPER) / `v4-smart` (IA EXPERT). Local AI names use short localized profile names; suffixes count every other configured matching profile and advance past names used by any human or AI (`Simple`, `Simple-1`, `Simple-2`), regardless of slot order. Names remain editable, frozen across language changes, and are not retroactively renumbered. Manual names must be unique after locale-independent `trim().toLowerCase()` normalization; duplicates are highlighted after blur/button interaction and block local start. Never use default-locale `toLocaleLowerCase()` for this comparison.
- Palette: `VGA_PALETTE` only (16 VGA + neon arcade extras).
- Tanks: `drawTankSprite` only, 24×15, slope tilt, independent turret. Active triangle, `ownerColor` shells, micro recoil.
- Phases: `MENU` → `COMBAT` → `RESOLUTION` → `CELEBRATION` → `SUMMARY` → `SHOP` → `GAME_OVER`.
- Shields & Gauges: 40 innate shield points per tank/round. Direct hits deal 2× damage to shield (absorbs via `Math.ceil(shield / 2)`; 1× overflow to health); indirect splash deals 1× damage. Fall damage directly reduces health, leaving shield intact. Visual gauge on Canvas: single dark cyan bar at $y-24$ when shield > 0 and health is full; stacked dual bars (dark cyan shield at $y-28$, green health at $y-23$, name at $y-36$) when shield > 0 and health < maxHealth; single green bar at $y-24$ when shield <= 0.
- Weapons: `WEAPON_REGISTRY` in `src/types/weapon.ts`. Missile unlimited, not in shop. Economy: exact per-shot calculator in `src/game/economy/`; $X = $3 / $3.50 / $4 for 2 / 3 / 4 players, one final ceiling, no self-reward. Floating `+amount$` lasts 3 seconds without blocking; summary = round gain, shop = total balance.
- Pricing: Baby Nuke (`NUKE`) costs $420; BULLDOZER $150 (0 HP / 0 blast, push + recoil, skips `applyExplosionDamage`). All shop and AI purchases derive from `WEAPON_REGISTRY`.
- Zeus Lightning: `src/game/zeus/` is a special anti-deadlock action, never a weapon. With ≥2 living AIs/no living human, `living AI × 5` shots without a paid hit (`hasEarnings`) appoint Zeus fairly. Reset on earnings/human/<2 survivors/Zeus death/round end; keep history across rounds. Consume the last living direct attacker except BULLDOZER, else injected RNG; kill only the target and pay `25X`. Never add `ZEUS_LIGHTNING` to weapon types/registry, `FireCommand`, shop, or `AIEngine`.
- Online (in `main`): protocol v1 temporarily normalizes/logs unversioned v0. Strict/v0 `FIRE` and authoritative `SHOT` share finite inclusive `FIRE_COMMAND_*` bounds (angle -360° to 360°, power 0 to 100), repeated defensively in `GameRoom.executeFire`; only unsupported numeric versions close in `4402`. Shop success acks `{ slot, actionId }`, and pending retries reuse the same ID until correlation. Deploy Worker first, require `/api/health` protocol 1/client minimum 0, then Pages; automatic production Pages deployment must be disabled. `VITE_HOTSEAT_ONLY=true` removes online from staging. Server owns turns, FIRE/ammo, shop, rewards and reconnect state; replay uses `authoritativeShotQueue.ts` + `DeferredTransitionBuffer`. Dev: `npm run dev` + `npm run worker:dev`.
- Zeus online is Durable Object-authoritative and persisted before broadcast through `ZEUS_APPOINTED`, `ZEUS_STRIKE`, `ZEUS_STRIKE_APPLIED`, and reconnect `ZEUS_STATE`. IDs are idempotent; economic failover has no effect; cosmetic geometry never consumes room RNG.
- Tests: **760** across **73** files. Version `0.7.0`.

## AI

All tank AI implements `AIEngine`. Router: `AIByProfileStrategy` in `GameCanvas.tsx`.

- `v1-random` / `AISimpleStrategy` — naive. Do not add `fallibleAim`. Early rounds alcoholic (`roundSkill`).
- `v2-heuristic` / `AIHeuristicStrategy` — first shot ≥ 36 px, lock at shot 5 (`SHOTS_TO_HIT`).
- `v3-sniper` / `AISniperStrategy` — first shot ≥ 36 px, lock at shot 4, 14 % slip after lock.
- `v4-smart` / `AISmartStrategy` — first shot ≥ 36 px, lock at shot 3.

v2–v4 share `fallibleAim.ts` + `roundSkill.ts` (ease-out warmup, late tighten), `terrainMaterialTactics.ts` (no DRILLER on ROCK; prefer DRILLER on SOFT when the default is MISSILE), and `bulldozerTactics.ts` (BULLDOZER on map edge / drop ≥ 12 px; v1 never buys or fires it). All AI share `hitReaction.ts` (Issue 174: direct hit +50%, fall 1–25% cumulative on shot 1; shot 2: Sniper 0%, Expert 12%, OK/Simple 25%; shot 3: 0%). New profile → new file under `game/entities/ai/`, register in the dispatcher. Never put AI in `TankManager` or `GameEngine`.

## Response

- Dry, production-ready. Paths, types, architecture — no fluff.
- Before finishing: `npm run lint && npm run build && npm run test`. Fix failures immediately. See [AGENTS.md § Verification](./AGENTS.md#verification-checklist).
- Do not edit rule files unless the user asked.

## Commit style

- Imperative mood.
- Sign with name + exact model.
